  <section id="sources">
    <h2>Sources</h2>
    <p>
      Dates are those printed on the work, or its year of publication. I have
      read the sections cited above, not every page of each work. Page numbers
      are as printed in each work. For the Akbulat article they are the PDF’s
      own page numbers. The ORSAM report’s text comes out of the PDF in a
      scrambled order, so allow a page either way for its page numbers.
      Mirzoeva and Apazheva and Lash are web texts with no page numbers.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li id="src-kazzaz">
        <strong>Gizem Kazzaz</strong>, <em>A Glimpse into the World of Muhajirs:
        Circassians in Ottoman Syria (1864&ndash;1910)</em>. MA thesis, Sabancı
        University (supervisor: Selçuk Akşin Somel). Approved
        <time datetime="2021-07-08">8 July 2021</time>. English. Quneitra and
        Mansura are covered in chapter 3 (pp. 24&ndash;37).
